            "review_title": "Review at Cafe Des Beaux Arts",
            "review_text": "Anh Amắn 🇻🇳\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam12939 contributions\n20\nOpulent Café & fabulous Art\nSep 2024 • Solo\nBased off the lobby of the wonderful Hôtel des Arts Saigon, this opulent and luxurious café is a fantastic place to either have a mid morning coffee or smoothies or even something stronger. The service is very polished. It really does want to make you check into the hotel if you are not already a guest.\n\nMy visit was for coffee followed by a viewing of the annual “The Flow of Heritage” exhibition, a celebration of Vietnamese culture hosted at Café des Beaux-Arts in the Hôtel des Arts Saigon.\n\nThis year the exhibition blended together art forms featuring the intricate lacquer paintings of Lại Thanh Dũng combined with ancient Vietnamese costumes of Hue - the ancient capital. Totally beautiful and mesmerizing. It seemed like a perfect marriage between the opulence of the café and the flow of the exhibition. Well done.\nRead more\nWritten September 26, 2024",
            "rating": 5.0,
